{"title":"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5ca1da04f81de5bbd50869c8aaccac1ca0caa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10z^2-3iz-k=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a complex variable and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56bfe567aec24da391224dc2f10e8cc4ef626dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^2=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />. Which of the following statements is true?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/987a960399aacbd7c8707fb19b5f9dec55a22da1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) For all positive real numbers k, both roots are pure imaginary} \\quad\\\\ \\text{(B) For all negative real numbers k, both roots are pure imaginary} \\quad\\\\ \\text{(C) For all pure imaginary numbers k, both roots are real and rational} \\quad\\\\ \\text{(D) For all pure imaginary numbers k, both roots are real and irrational} \\quad\\\\ \\text{(E) For all complex numbers k, neither root is real}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"527\" height=\"96\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> denote the roots of the polynomial.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff031b5e65378d63b5e3f2acd8c374c75917916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 + r_2 = \\dfrac{3i}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"39\" /> is pure imaginary, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> have offsetting real parts.  Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2aeffd4171d5cda152c9080a22ba80785df52989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 = a + bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa8da06d95bc9351e00a28c95b865ccc1527dbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2 = -a + ci$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />.  \n</p><p>Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/650a1a143cdbe404b8305a7c68433c40cad8da5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-k = r_1 r_2 = -a^2 -bc + a(c-b)i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"262\" height=\"19\" />.  In the case that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is real, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1332e35f8cc455b38f178b065d8e6b0bbb2531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(c-b)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> so either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69cefa6855d2216036df094012f7ad2a7e4e204f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> or that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebda5306c70a24c574ef0107ed5b5152b5f594cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=c$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.  In the first case, the roots are pure imaginary and in the second case we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b282dde80a735576a1c4f9e3935840f3b5227a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = a^2+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />, a positive number.\n</p><p>We can therefore conclude that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is real and negative, it must be the first case and the roots are pure imaginary.\n</p><p>It's possible to rule out the other cases by reasoning through the cases, but this is enough to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c3218ca790f4eac4048f34f68433655b19e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" /> is true.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME\" title=\"1993 AHSME\">1993 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1993 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1993\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1993_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1993 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183617\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 163/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2494/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 152/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3753/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.701   